lines=['# Training exposure, geometry and context analysis','','Replayed all 80,000 cached training spheres for each sampler (40 epochs). Used exact cached centers/jitter, the assigned training partition, radius 2 m, nearest-15,000 valid-point cap, and excluded padding. The mixed sampler totals match its pre-existing diagnostic exactly. No model weights were changed and no training was launched.','','## What class-mix actually changes','','| Class | Spatial valid-point visits | Class-mix valid-point visits | Change |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
a=s['samplers']['spatial']['class_point_exposure'];b=s['samplers']['classmix']['class_point_exposure']
for i,name in enumerate(names):lines.append(f'| {name} | {a[i]:,} | {b[i]:,} | {(b[i]/a[i]-1)*100:+.2f}% |')
lines+=['','The strongest effect is extra pump exposure, consistent with the pump recall gain. Tank exposure increases modestly despite 23.2% more tank centers: center class is not the same as the class composition of a sphere. The tank-center mean composition is almost unchanged (86.77% tank before, 86.73% after; roughly 12% pipe in both). I-beam-centered spheres remain about 65% i-beam and 34% rectangular beam. There is no large shift in mean context composition for these centers.','','## Coverage becomes slightly less complete for tanks','','Area 2 contains all training tanks. Of 67,651 subsampled tank points:','','| Quantity | Spatial | Class-mix |','|---|---:|---:|']
